EXPERIMENT 5
Queries using ANY, ALL, IN, EXISTS, NOT EXISTS, UNION, INTERSECT

AIM
To write and execute SQL queries using ANY, ALL, IN, EXISTS, and NOT EXISTS, set operations UNION and INTERSECT, and integrity constraints on related tables.

THEORY
IN checks membership in a list or subquery. ANY is true when a comparison holds for at least one returned value; ALL requires it to hold for every value. EXISTS tests whether a subquery returns rows; NOT EXISTS tests whether it returns none. UNION combines results and removes duplicates; UNION ALL retains duplicates; INTERSECT returns common rows. Participating SELECT statements must return the same number of compatible columns.

PROCEDURE
Create Department, Student, Course, and Enrollment tables; insert sample data; execute the subqueries and set operations; then test constraint violations.

RESULT
The operators and set operations are demonstrated using the related sample tables.

